---

<BaseLayout
  title="613Flea - Brand and Web Case Study"
  description="613Flea is a responsive brand and website redesign for an Ottawa indoor marketplace, focused on visual identity, vendor discovery, visitor planning, and community engagement."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="project-detail flea-page">
    <section class="project-hero site-shell section">
      <a href="/#work" class="project-back-link">← Work</a>

      <div class="project-hero__intro">
        <p class="project-number">{project?.number ?? "02"}</p>

        <div>
          <p class="project-label">Brand + Web - 2025</p>
          <h1>613Flea</h1>

          <p class="project-hero__summary">
            613Flea is a not-for-profit Ottawa marketplace redesigned with a clearer brand identity
            and a more engaging digital experience for visitors and vendors.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="project-hero__image flea-hero-card">
  <img
    class="flea-hero-card__main"
    src="/images/projects/613flea/hero.png"
    alt="613Flea redesigned website hero mockup"
  />

  <figcaption class="flea-existing-site-mini-card">
    <div class="flea-existing-site-mini-card__label">
      <span>Existing Website</span>
      <small>Before redesign</small>
    </div>

    <img
      src="/images/projects/613flea/existing-website.png"
      alt="Original 613Flea website homepage before redesign"
    />

    <p>
      The original homepage had a handmade market feel, but needed clearer hierarchy,
      stronger visual structure, and a more flexible brand system.
    </p>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

      <dl class="project-facts">
  <div>
    <dt>Role</dt>
    <dd>Product Designer, 4-person team</dd>
  </div>

  <div>
    <dt>Contribution</dt>
    <dd>
      Led the homepage redesign and visual direction; contributed to branding,
      research, prototyping, testing, client communication, and creative brief design.
    </dd>
  </div>

  <div>
    <dt>Tools</dt>
    <dd>Figma, FigJam, Basecamp, Maze</dd>
  </div>

  <div>
    <dt>Timeframe</dt>
    <dd>May - Aug 2025</dd>
  </div>

  <div>
    <dt>Year</dt>
    <dd>2025</dd>
  </div>
</dl>
      <section class="flea-test-results" aria-labelledby="flea-test-results-title">
        <h2 id="flea-test-results-title">USABILITY TEST RESULTS</h2>
        <p class="flea-test-results__context">2 rounds of Maze usability testing · 12 participants in Round 1 · 16 after iteration</p>
        <dl class="flea-test-results__metrics">
          <div>
            <dt>Event information task</dt>
            <dd>75% → 100%</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Vendor discovery task</dt>
            <dd>75% → 95%</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Vendor application task</dt>
            <dd>100%</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>
    </section>

    <section class="project-section site-shell">
      <div class="project-section__label">
        <p>01 / The Problem</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section__content">
        <p class="project-lead">
          At the time of the redesign, 613Flea already had a strong local presence, but its website and branding did not fully reflect the energy of the market. The visual identity was inconsistent, visitor information lacked a clear structure, and there was little opportunity to discover vendors before attending.
        </p>

        <div class="number-list">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>

            <div>
              <h3>The brand lacked a consistent system</h3>
              <p>
                The existing identity had character, but it was difficult to apply consistently across the website and other brand materials.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>02</span>

            <div>
              <h3>Visitor information had no clear home</h3>
              <p>
                Event dates were available, but practical visitor details such as parking, accessibility, and planning information were not grouped into an obvious visitor section.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>03</span>

            <div>
              <h3>Vendor discovery was limited</h3>
              <p>
                Visitors had little opportunity to explore vendors before attending the market.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="question-block">
          <h3>The Goal</h3>
          <p>
                Refresh the 613Flea brand and website while keeping its local character, making visitor information easier to access and giving people a better way to discover vendors before market day.
              </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-section site-shell">
  <div class="project-section__label">
    <p>02 / Research</p>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section__content">
    <p class="project-lead">
      Research focused on understanding 613Flea’s brand, audience, competitors, and the gaps in the current website.
    </p>

    <h3 class="subheading">Creative Brief</h3>
    <p class="project-copy">
      A detailed creative brief was created to define the audience, brand direction, project goals, and website needs. I designed the final brief document used to organize and present the research.
    </p>

    <h4 class="flea-brief-priorities-heading">Key priorities from the brief</h4>
    <div class="split-copy">
      <article><h3>Keep 613Flea’s local character</h3></article>
      <article><h3>Make visitor information easier to access</h3></article>
      <article><h3>Improve vendor discovery</h3></article>
      <article><h3>Build a more consistent brand</h3></article>
    </div>
    <a
      class="prototype-link"
      href={creativeBriefUrl}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer"
    >
      View Full Creative Brief PDF ↗
    </a>
    <h3 class="subheading">Competitive Review</h3>
    <p class="project-copy">
      A competitor review looked at how other marketplaces handled event information, vendor discovery, branding, and visitor planning.
    </p>
    <div class="flea-competitor-grid">
      {competitorAnalysis.map((competitor) => (
        <article class="flea-competitor-card">
          <header>
            <div class={`flea-competitor-card__logo ${competitor.logoClass ?? ""}`}>
              <img src={competitor.logo} alt={`${competitor.name} logo`} />
            </div>


            <h3>{competitor.name}</h3>
          </header>

          <section>
            <h4>What works</h4>
            <p>{competitor.works}</p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h4>Gap / opportunity</h4>
            <p>{competitor.gap}</p>
          </section>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h3 class="subheading flea-research-summary-heading">What This Pointed To</h3>
    <p class="project-copy">Together, the brief and competitor review highlighted three areas to focus on in the redesign.</p>
    <div class="research-list flea-research-summary">
      <article>
        <h3>Clearer visit planning</h3>
        <p>Visitor information needed a clearer place in the website structure.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Better vendor discovery</h3>
        <p>Visitors needed more ways to explore vendors before market day.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Stronger digital identity</h3>
        <p>The website needed to feel more like the lively, local experience of the physical market.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <h3 class="subheading">Audience Focus</h3>
    <p class="project-copy">The redesign also needed to work for three practical groups: people discovering the market, vendors looking to participate, and visitors planning their first trip.</p>
    <div class="flea-audience-focus">
      <article>
        <h4>Local visitors</h4>
        <p>Want to understand what is happening and discover vendors before attending.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h4>Vendors</h4>
        <p>Need clear application information and better visibility.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h4>First-time visitors</h4>
        <p>Need practical details to plan their visit with confidence.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
    <section class="project-section site-shell">
  <div class="project-section__label">
    <p>03 / From Needs to Solutions</p>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section__content">
    <p class="project-lead">
      The audience needs identified during research were translated into three design responses that shaped the redesign.
    </p>

    <div class="flea-response-grid">
      {userSolutions.map((item) => (
        <article class="flea-response-card">
          <header>
            <span class="flea-response-card__number" aria-hidden="true">{item.number}</span>
            <h3>{item.user}</h3>
          </header>
          <div class="flea-response-card__need">
            <h4 class="flea-response-card__label">Need</h4>
            <p>{item.problem}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flea-response-card__response">
            <h4 class="flea-response-card__label">Design response</h4>
            <h5>{item.title}</h5>
            <p>{item.solution}</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-section site-shell">
      <div class="project-section__label">
        <p>04 / Structure</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section__content">
        <p class="project-lead">
          The website was organized around five core areas: Home [1.0], Event Calendar [2.0], Vendor Directory [3.0], Become a Vendor [4.0], and Visitor Info [5.0].
        </p>

        <p class="project-copy">
          This keeps visitor planning and vendor discovery close to the homepage while giving vendors a clear path to application information.
        </p>

        <figure class="project-figure">
          <img src="/images/projects/613flea/sitemap.png" alt="613Flea sitemap" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-section site-shell">
      <div class="project-section__label">
        <p>05 / Early Design</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-section__content">
        <p class="project-lead">
          Low-fidelity wireframes were used to translate the sitemap into responsive desktop and mobile layouts, focusing on hierarchy and access to the information identified during research.
        </p>

        <div class="flea-early-focus">
          <article>
            <h3>Event visibility</h3>
            <p>Upcoming market information was given stronger hierarchy.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Vendor discovery</h3>
            <p>A clearer path was created for browsing vendors before attending.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Visitor planning</h3>
            <p>Practical visit information was grouped into a dedicated area.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <h3 class="subheading">Low-Fidelity Wireframes</h3>
        <figure class="project-figure flea-lowfi-overview">
          <button type="button" class="flea-board-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="View 613Flea low-fidelity wireframes at full size">
            <img src="/images/projects/613flea/low-fi.png" alt="613Flea low fidelity wireframes" loading="lazy" />
          </button>
          <figcaption>Click to view full size</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-section site-shell">
  <div class="project-section__label">
    <p>06 / Visual Direction</p>
